mode: "100644"
text: "# Escalation, Pause the Queue & Safety\n\nThe high-stakes operational core: who decides, the one real WoopSocial action in a crisis, and the\nrules that keep an AI agent in its lane when things are on fire.\n\n## Human-in-the-loop (non-negotiable)\n\nA crisis is exactly when the agent **must not act autonomously.** The split:\n\n- **The agent:** triages severity, **drafts** holding statements/responses in **approved brand-voice\n  language**, suggests moderation actions, helps **pause the queue**, and flags what to escalate.\n- **The human** (and, for high-severity, **legal + leadership + PR professionals**): **approves and\n  posts** every public word, makes the judgment calls, and does the **in-platform moderation**.\n- **Never auto-respond to a crisis. Never fabricate facts. Never apologize for the unverified.** Never\n  speak beyond authorized language.\n\n## The approval chain / escalation paths\n\nDecide *before* you need it (and apply in the moment):\n\n- **Low** → social/community handles it with care.\n- **Medium** → loop in PR + support; a measured response with approved wording.\n- **High** → **escalate to legal review + executive visibility**; use trained spokespeople and\n  **pre-approved language**. For legal, safety, regulatory, or serious-harm matters, **involve\n  professionals** — this skill is not a substitute for legal counsel.\n\nIf unsure whether to escalate, **escalate.** The cost of an extra human review is small; the cost of an\nagent freelancing a high-severity response is not.\n\n## Pause the queue (the real WoopSocial action)\n\nThis is the one concrete, honest thing WoopSocial does in a crisis. During a crisis **or a sensitive\nnews moment** (a tragedy, disaster, public mourning), your scheduled promo posts can publish\nautomatically and make you look tone-deaf. So:\n\n- **Pause / reschedule the scheduled posts** before they fire — via `scheduling-and-queue` (WoopSocial\n  can **delete or reschedule** pending posts; there's no in-place edit, so it's delete-and-recreate).\n- **Confirm with the human** which posts to hold and for how long (the confirmation contract from\n  `scheduling-and-queue`).\n- **Resume** deliberately when the moment has passed.\n\nThis is genuinely useful and fully within WoopSocial's real capabilities — surface it early in any\nsensitive moment.\n\n## What WoopSocial can and can't do here (honest scope)\n\n- **Can:** publish/schedule, and **pause/delete/reschedule your own posts** (the queue).\n- **Cannot:** hide or delete others' comments, block users, pull mentions/DMs, monitor, listen, or show\n  analytics. There's **no inbox/moderation/listening surface.** Monitoring and moderation happen via\n  the **platform's native tools** (and third-party listening tools), done by the **human**.\n\nNever imply WoopSocial monitors mentions, manages an inbox, or moderates.\n\n## Wellbeing (a crisis is stressful)\n\n- **Designate responders and windows** — don't let everyone doomscroll the pile-on; assign who watches\n  and who drafts.\n- **Protect the people** — a coordinated attack is draining; step back, don't engage every troll, lean\n  on the team.\n- **Genuine only** — don't fight a pile-on with bought support, sockpuppets, or fake positivity; it\n  backfires. Real, calm, factual responses win.\n"
